      "Modular Avatar merges the outfit's bones into the avatar's bones automatically, <strong>only when you upload or press Play in Unity</strong> (Merge Armature). The avatar and outfit you edit stay as they are, so nothing gets broken. To remove the outfit, just delete it from the Hierarchy.",
    ],
    route: [
      { head: "Put the outfit inside the avatar", note: "Drag it in the Hierarchy" },
      { head: "Setup Outfit", note: "Adds Merge Armature" },
      { head: "Play or upload", note: "Bones are merged automatically" },
      { head: "Moves with the body", note: "Your original data stays as is" },
    ],
    installTitle: "Add Modular Avatar",
    installLead: `Add Modular Avatar to your project with VCC or ALCOM. How to install VCC and ALCOM is covered in <a href="${prefix}/avatar-tips/setup/">${tipNo("setup")}</a>.`,
    install: [
      `On the ${ext(maDocs, "Modular Avatar website")}, go to "Installation". If you use VCC, press "Add Modular Avatar to VCC". If you use ALCOM, enter <code>https://vpm.nadena.dev/vpm.json</code> under "Add VPM Repository".`,
      "Open your project with \"Manage Project\" in VCC or \"Manage\" in ALCOM, and press the + next to Modular Avatar to add it.",
    ],
    stepsTitle: "Steps to dress your avatar",
    steps: [
      "Drag the outfit's unitypackage into Unity's Project window and press \"Import\".",
      "In the outfit's folder, find the prefab with your avatar's name. Outfits often have a separate prefab for each supported avatar.",
      "Drag that prefab onto your avatar in the Hierarchy (the object with the VRC Avatar Descriptor) to make it a child of the avatar.",
      "Right-click the outfit and choose <code>[ModularAvatar] Setup Outfit</code>.",
      "Turn off the clothes the avatar was wearing (uncheck the box at the top left of the Inspector).",
      "Press Unity's Play button, and check that the clothes follow the avatar when it moves.",
    ],
    hierarchyMock: {
      variant: "unity",
      caption: "Recreated view: Unity's Hierarchy, and the menu when you right-click the outfit. Names are examples.",
      screens: [
        {
          bar: "Hierarchy",
          label: "Recreated view of the Hierarchy. Under the avatar Avatar_A are Armature, Body, the original clothes Default_Outfit, and 1 the new outfit Dress_for_Avatar_A",
          rows: [
            { label: "▼ Avatar_A", type: "text" },
            { label: "　▶ Armature", type: "text" },
            { label: "　Body", type: "text" },
            { label: "　Default_Outfit", type: "text" },
            { mark: 1, label: "　▶ Dress_for_Avatar_A", type: "text", hot: true },
          ],
        },
        {
          bar: "Right-click menu",
          label: "Recreated view of the menu when you right-click the outfit. It has 2 [ModularAvatar] Setup Outfit",
          rows: [
            { label: "Copy", type: "text" },
            { label: "Paste", type: "text" },
            { label: "Rename", type: "text" },
            { label: "Duplicate", type: "text" },
            { mark: 2, label: "[ModularAvatar] Setup Outfit", type: "text", hot: true },
          ],
        },
      ],
      notes: [
        "Put the outfit's prefab directly under the avatar (as its child). Don't put it outside the avatar or inside the Armature.",
        "Right-click the outfit and choose this. It finds the Armature inside the outfit and adds Merge Armature to it.",
      ],
    },
    mergeTitle: "What Setup Outfit does",
    merge: [
      "When you choose Setup Outfit, <strong>MA Merge Armature</strong> is added to the Armature inside the outfit, and <strong>MA Outfit Root</strong> is added to the top of the outfit.",
      "Merge Armature finds the outfit's bones by name and merges them into the avatar's bones with the same names. Bones the avatar doesn't have (such as skirt bones) are added as children of the avatar's bones. The outfit's swaying parts (PhysBones) are also fixed so they move the bones they were merged into.",
      "The merge happens only when you press Play and when you upload. When you stop playing, the Hierarchy goes back to how it was.",
    ],
    mergeMock: {
      variant: "unity",
      caption: "Recreated view: MA Merge Armature on the outfit's Armature. The layout is simplified.",
      screens: [{
        bar: "Inspector › Armature (inside Dress_for_Avatar_A)",
        label: "Recreated view of MA Merge Armature. 1 Merge Target is Armature, then Prefix and Suffix, 2 Position sync mode is Avatar to Target (Unidirectional), 3 Avoid name collisions is checked",
        rows: [
          { type: "head", text: "▼ MA Merge Armature" },
          { mark: 1, label: "Merge Target", type: "select", text: "Armature (Transform)", hot: true },
          { label: "Prefix", type: "value", text: "" },
          { label: "Suffix", type: "value", text: "" },
          { mark: 2, label: "Position sync mode", type: "select", text: "Avatar =====&gt; Target (Unidirectional)" },
          { mark: 3, type: "check", on: true, text: "Avoid name collisions" },
        ],
      }],
      notes: [
        "Where the outfit's bones are merged. The avatar's Armature goes here. Setup Outfit fills it in for you, so you normally don't change it.",
        "Makes the outfit follow the avatar's pose while you edit. Setup Outfit sets it to this one-way mode.",
        "Renames the bones the avatar doesn't have, so they don't clash with bones from other items.",
      ],
    },
    shrinkTitle: "When your body pokes through the clothes",
    shrink: [
      "If the body is bigger than the clothes, your skin pokes through them when you move. Many avatars have BlendShapes (shape keys) that shrink or hide the body under the clothes. They have names like <code>Shrink_...</code> or <code>Hide_...</code>, and they are listed in the avatar's manual.",
      "Raise the value of that BlendShape on Body's Skinned Mesh Renderer to shrink it. But the value stays the same even when you take the clothes off. Also, if the avatar's FX Animator writes to this BlendShape, VRChat changes it back from the value you set in Unity (<a href=\"" + prefix + "/avatar-tips/unity-vs-vrchat/\">" + tipNo("unity-vs-vrchat") + "</a>).",
      "We recommend adding <strong>MA Shape Changer</strong> inside the outfit. It sets the body's BlendShape to a value you choose only while the outfit is on. When you turn the outfit off, the body goes back to normal. With Delete, it can also remove the body's polygons under the clothes to make the avatar lighter.",
    ],
    shapeMock: {
      variant: "unity",
      caption: "Recreated view: MA Shape Changer added inside the outfit. BlendShape names are examples.",
      screens: [{
        bar: "Inspector › Dress (inside Dress_for_Avatar_A)",
        label: "Recreated view of MA Shape Changer. 1 Target Renderer is Body, 2 Shrink_Chest is Set to 100, 3 Hide_Belly is Delete",
        rows: [
          { type: "head", text: "▼ MA Shape Changer" },
          { mark: 1, label: "Target Renderer", type: "select", text: "Body (Skinned Mesh Renderer)", hot: true },
          { mark: 2, label: "Shrink_Chest", type: "seg", options: ["Set", "Delete"], active: 0 },
          { label: "Value", type: "slider", value: 100, text: "100" },
          { mark: 3, label: "Hide_Belly", type: "seg", options: ["Set", "Delete"], active: 1 },
        ],
      }],
      notes: [
        "Put in the body mesh you want to shrink (usually Body).",
        "Set uses this value while the outfit is on. Use it for BlendShapes that shrink the body.",
        "Delete removes the part this BlendShape affects while the outfit is on. Use it for parts the clothes hide completely.",
      ],
    },
    demoTitle: "Try it yourself",
    demoLead: "Change the shrink value and how it is applied, and compare how the body looks with the clothes on and off. Assume the FX Animator doesn't write to this BlendShape.",
    demo: {
      wear: "With clothes on",
      nude: "With clothes off",
      slider: "Body shrink (Shrink)",
      mode: "How to shrink",
      modes: [
        { value: "unity", text: "Set the value on Body's BlendShape" },
        { value: "changer", text: "Add MA Shape Changer to the outfit" },
      ],
      whyUnity: "A value set on Body stays the same whether the clothes are on or off.",
      whyChanger: "Shape Changer sets the value only while the outfit is on. It goes back to 0 when you take it off.",
      poke: "With clothes on: the body pokes through the clothes. Raise the value.",
      fit: "With clothes on: the body fits inside the clothes.",
      stay: "With clothes off: the body stays shrunk ({v}).",
      back: "With clothes off: the body goes back to its original shape.",
      noJs: "Turn on JavaScript to use this figure.",
    },
    menuTitle: "Put clothes on and off from the menu",
    menuLead: "With Modular Avatar, you can add an outfit on/off switch to the Expressions Menu (Action Menu) without building an Animator yourself.",
    menuMore: `To build the Animator yourself and make the on/off logic from scratch, see <a href="${prefix}/avatar-tips/toggle/">${tipNo("toggle")} ${tip("toggle").title.en}</a>.`,
    menu: [
      "Right-click the avatar in the Hierarchy and choose <code>Modular Avatar → Create Toggle</code>. An object with Menu Item, Menu Installer and Object Toggle is created as a child of the avatar.",
      "Rename the object to the name you want in the menu (for example, \"Dress\"). This name becomes the menu item's name.",
      "Press + in Object Toggle and drag the outfit object in. With the checkbox on the right checked, it turns on when selected. Unchecked, it turns off when selected.",
      "If the avatar wears these clothes from the start, turn on \"Is Default\" in Menu Item so it starts on.",
      "The Shape Changer inside the outfit follows the outfit's on/off state. When you take the outfit off, the body goes back to normal.",
    ],
    testTitle: "Test it in Play mode",
    test: [
      "When you press Unity's Play button, Modular Avatar merges the outfit. Move the avatar's pose in the Scene and check that the clothes follow and nothing pokes through.",
      "If you install Gesture Manager, you can open the Expressions Menu during Play and test the outfit on/off too.",
      "If it all looks good, upload and check in VRChat as well. In front of a mirror, try big moves like crouching and raising your arms.",
    ],
    casesTitle: "Common problems",
    caseLabels: { symptom: "What happens", cause: "Cause", fix: "Fix" },
    cases: [
      { title: "The clothes don't follow",
        symptom: "When you press Play or move in VRChat, the clothes stay where they are.",
        cause: "You haven't run Setup Outfit, or the outfit isn't a child of the avatar.",
        fix: "Put the outfit directly under the avatar, then right-click it and run Setup Outfit again. Also check that MA Merge Armature is on the outfit's Armature." },
      { title: "The body pokes through the clothes",
        symptom: "When you move, the skin on the chest, belly or thighs shows outside the clothes.",
        cause: "The body under the clothes is still at full size.",
        fix: "Add the BlendShape that shrinks the body to the outfit with MA Shape Changer. If you set the value directly on Body, also check that the FX Animator doesn't write to it (" + tipNo("unity-vs-vrchat") + ")." },
      { title: "The clothes float or don't fit",
        symptom: "The clothes float away from the body. The sleeves or hem are the wrong length.",
        cause: "You are using a prefab for a different avatar, or you changed your avatar's body shape.",
        fix: "Check that the prefab is for your avatar. If you changed the body shape with BlendShapes, set the same BlendShapes on the outfit, or use MA Blendshape Sync to keep them at the same value." },
      { title: "Swaying parts are applied twice",
        symptom: "The chest or hair sways strangely. It bounces or shakes.",
        cause: "The outfit and the avatar may both have PhysBones that move the same bones.",
        fix: "Read the outfit's manual, decide which PhysBones to use, and delete or turn off the ones you don't need." },
      { title: "The menu doesn't show up",
        symptom: "The toggle you made doesn't appear in the Expressions Menu.",
        cause: "There is no Menu Installer, or the toggle object is outside the avatar. The menu may also be full.",
        fix: "Put the toggle under the avatar as its child, and check that it has a Menu Installer. Also test it in Play mode with Gesture Manager." },
      { title: "The clothes turn pink",
        symptom: "The outfit's clothes show up in solid pink.",
        cause: "The shader the outfit uses isn't in your project.",
        fix: "Add the shader named in the manual (such as lilToon). If it still doesn't work, choose the shader on the material again." },
      { title: "You want to put the outfit on an unsupported avatar",
        symptom: "An outfit you like doesn't support your avatar.",
        cause: "The body shape and bone positions are different, so it doesn't fit as is.",
        fix: "First line it up roughly with \"Reset position to base avatar\" on the Outfit Root, then fix the bone positions and sizes bit by bit. There are also tools to help you fit it. This takes time, so try it after you are used to editing avatars. Also check that the terms of use allow edits for unsupported avatars." },
    ],
    careTitle: "Things to watch out for",
    care: [
      "You don't need to unpack the outfit or avatar prefabs. Leaving them packed makes updates easier.",
      "Turn off the original clothes instead of deleting them, so you can bring them back later.",
      "Adding an outfit increases polygons and materials, and can lower your performance rank. Check it before you upload.",
      "Back up your project before you edit, just to be safe.",
    ],
    sumTitle: "Summary",
    sum: [
      "Put the prefab made for your avatar under the avatar as its child.",
      "Right-click and choose Setup Outfit, and Modular Avatar merges the bones automatically. Your original data isn't broken.",
      "To stop the body poking through, use MA Shape Changer to shrink the body only while the outfit is on.",
      "With Create Toggle, you can put the clothes on and off from the menu.",
    ],
    back: "All Avatar Tips",
  },
}[pageLocale];
const sections = [
  { id: "when", title: l.whenTitle },
  { id: "before", title: l.beforeTitle },
  { id: "why", title: l.whyTitle },
  { id: "install", title: l.installTitle },
  { id: "steps", title: l.stepsTitle },
  { id: "merge", title: l.mergeTitle },
  { id: "shrink", title: l.shrinkTitle },
  { id: "demo", title: l.demoTitle },
  { id: "menu", title: l.menuTitle },
  { id: "test", title: l.testTitle },
  { id: "cases", title: l.casesTitle },
  { id: "care", title: l.careTitle },
  { id: "summary", title: l.sumTitle },
];
%><article class="article_1" aria-labelledby="article-heading">
  <header class="section_2 page_1 article_1__header">
    <p class="article_1__series"><a href="<%= prefix %>/avatar-tips/"><%= l.series %></a></p>
    <h1 class="page_1__h1" id="article-heading"><%= l.title %></h1>
    <p class="article_1__lead"><%= l.lead %></p>
    <p class="section_2__note"><%= l.publishedLabel %> <time datetime="<%= article.published %>"><%= published %></time> · <%= l.meta %></p>
    <nav class="jump_1" aria-label="<%= l.tocLabel %>">
      <ul>
        <% sections.forEach(function (s) { %>
          <li><a href="#<%= s.id %>"><%= s.title %></a></li>
        <% }); %>
      </ul>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <section class="section_2 article_1__section" id="when" aria-labelledby="when-heading">
    <h2 class="section_2__h1" id="when-heading"><%= l.whenTitle %></h2>
    <ul class="rules_1">
      <% l.when.forEach(function (item) { %><li><%= item %></li><% }); %>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section_2 article_1__section" id="before" aria-labelledby="before-heading">
    <h2 class="section_2__h1" id="before-heading"><%= l.beforeTitle %></h2>
    <p class="article_1__p"><%= l.beforeLead %></p>
    <dl class="examples_1 examples_1--grid">
      <% l.before.forEach(function (item) { %>
        <div class="examples_1__item">
          <dt><%= item.head %></dt>
          <dd><%- item.body %></dd>
        </div>
      <% }); %>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="section_2 article_1__section" id="why" aria-labelledby="why-heading">
    <h2 class="section_2__h1" id="why-heading"><%= l.whyTitle %></h2>
    <% l.why.forEach(function (text) { %><p class="article_1__p"><%- text %></p><% }); %>
    <ol class="route_1">
      <% l.route.forEach(function (step) { %>
        <li class="route_1__step"><span class="route_1__head"><%= step.head %></span><span class="route_1__note"><%= step.note %></span></li>
      <% }); %>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="section_2 article_1__section" id="install" aria-labelledby="install-heading">
    <h2 class="section_2__h1" id="install-heading"><%= l.installTitle %></h2>
    <p class="article_1__p"><%- l.installLead %></p>
    <ol class="steps_1">
      <% l.install.forEach(function (step) { %><li><%- step %></li><% }); %>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="section_2 article_1__section" id="steps" aria-labelledby="steps-heading">
    <h2 class="section_2__h1" id="steps-heading"><%= l.stepsTitle %></h2>
    <ol class="steps_1">
      <% l.steps.forEach(function (step) { %><li><%- step %></li><% }); %>
    </ol>
    <%- include("_mock", { mock: l.hierarchyMock }) %>
  </section>

  <section class="section_2 article_1__section" id="merge" aria-labelledby="merge-heading">
    <h2 class="section_2__h1" id="merge-heading"><%= l.mergeTitle %></h2>
    <% l.merge.forEach(function (text) { %><p class="article_1__p"><%- text %></p><% }); %>
    <%- include("_mock", { mock: l.mergeMock }) %>
  </section>

  <section class="section_2 article_1__section" id="shrink" aria-labelledby="shrink-heading">
    <h2 class="section_2__h1" id="shrink-heading"><%= l.shrinkTitle %></h2>
    <% l.shrink.forEach(function (text) { %><p class="article_1__p"><%- text %></p><% }); %>
    <%- include("_mock", { mock: l.shapeMock }) %>
  </section>

  <section class="section_2 article_1__section" id="demo" aria-labelledby="demo-heading">
    <h2 class="section_2__h1" id="demo-heading"><%= l.demoTitle %></h2>
    <p class="article_1__p"><%= l.demoLead %></p>
    <div class="demo_2 js_outfit_demo"
      data-why-unity="<%= l.demo.whyUnity %>" data-why-changer="<%= l.demo.whyChanger %>"
      data-poke="<%= l.demo.poke %>" data-fit="<%= l.demo.fit %>"
      data-stay="<%= l.demo.stay %>" data-back="<%= l.demo.back %>">
      <div class="demo_2__faces">
        <div class="demo_2__face">
          <p class="demo_2__who"><%= l.demo.wear %></p>
          <div class="js_outfit_figure" data-wear="1"><%- figure(0, true) %></div>
          <p class="demo_2__num">Shrink <span class="js_outfit_num" data-wear="1">0</span></p>
        </div>
        <div class="demo_2__face">
          <p class="demo_2__who"><%= l.demo.nude %></p>
          <div class="js_outfit_figure" data-wear="0"><%- figure(0, false) %></div>
          <p class="demo_2__num">Shrink <span class="js_outfit_num" data-wear="0">0</span></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="demo_2__controls">
        <div class="demo_1__range">
          <p class="demo_1__label"><label for="outfit-shrink"><%= l.demo.slider %></label> <output class="demo_1__value" for="outfit-shrink">0</output></p>
          <input type="range" min="0" max="100" step="10" value="0" id="outfit-shrink" class="js_outfit_shrink">
        </div>
        <fieldset class="demo_1__distance">
          <legend class="demo_1__label"><%= l.demo.mode %></legend>
          <% l.demo.modes.forEach(function (m, i) { %>
            <label><input type="radio" name="outfit-mode" value="<%= m.value %>" class="js_outfit_mode"<% if (i === 0) { %> checked<% } %>> <%= m.text %></label>
          <% }); %>
        </fieldset>
      </div>
      <div class="demo_2__output" aria-live="polite">
        <p class="demo_1__why js_outfit_why"><%= l.demo.whyUnity %></p>
        <p class="demo_1__result is_ng js_outfit_result" data-wear="1"><%= l.demo.poke %></p>
        <p class="demo_1__result is_ok js_outfit_result" data-wear="0"><%= l.demo.back %></p>
      </div>
      <noscript><p class="section_2__note"><%= l.demo.noJs %></p></noscript>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section_2 article_1__section" id="menu" aria-labelledby="menu-heading">
    <h2 class="section_2__h1" id="menu-heading"><%= l.menuTitle %></h2>
    <p class="article_1__p"><%= l.menuLead %></p>
    <ol class="steps_1">
      <% l.menu.forEach(function (step) { %><li><%- step %></li><% }); %>
    </ol>
    <p class="article_1__p"><%- l.menuMore %></p>
  </section>

  <section class="section_2 article_1__section" id="test" aria-labelledby="test-heading">
    <h2 class="section_2__h1" id="test-heading"><%= l.testTitle %></h2>
    <ul class="rules_1">
      <% l.test.forEach(function (item) { %><li><%= item %></li><% }); %>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section_2 article_1__section" id="cases" aria-labelledby="cases-heading">
    <h2 class="section_2__h1" id="cases-heading"><%= l.casesTitle %></h2>
    <div class="case_1">
      <% l.cases.forEach(function (c) { %>
        <section class="case_1__item">
          <h3 class="case_1__title"><%= c.title %></h3>
          <dl class="case_1__list">
            <div><dt><%= l.caseLabels.symptom %></dt><dd><%= c.symptom %></dd></div>
            <div><dt><%= l.caseLabels.cause %></dt><dd><%= c.cause %></dd></div>
            <div><dt><%= l.caseLabels.fix %></dt><dd><%= c.fix %></dd></div>
          </dl>
        </section>
      <% }); %>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section_2 article_1__section" id="care" aria-labelledby="care-heading">
    <h2 class="section_2__h1" id="care-heading"><%= l.careTitle %></h2>
    <ul class="rules_1">
      <% l.care.forEach(function (item) { %><li><%= item %></li><% }); %>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section_2 article_1__section" id="summary" aria-labelledby="summary-heading">
    <h2 class="section_2__h1" id="summary-heading"><%= l.sumTitle %></h2>
    <ul class="rules_1">
      <% l.sum.forEach(function (item) { %><li><%= item %></li><% }); %>
    </ul>
    <p class="section_2__more"><a href="<%= prefix %>/avatar-tips/"><%= l.back %></a></p>
  </section>
</article>
